{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Consumption [שחפת].</b> Some say they are types of diseases." "<b>Fever [קדחת].</b> Every day. Derived from כי אש קדח' באפי (Numbers 11:1). And מהומה ומגערת ושחפת וקדחת ודלקת are descriptive nouns." "And the meaning of <b>ובדלקת.</b> is a third or fourth [disease]." "<b>ובחרחור [and with scorching].</b> Derived from וחרה נחושת׳ (Leviticus 26:19 — the bronze [sky] glows)." "<b>ובחרב [and with sword].</b> Derived from חורב [Horeb]." "<b>ובשדפון [and with blight].</b> Blights [נפיחות]; thus שדופות קדים (Jonah 4:8). Some say the opposite, and the meaning is emaciation [דקוק]." "<b>ובירקון [and with mildew].</b> As it sounds in the language of Kedar. And some say that these are diseases of grain, and שדפון is like שדופות קדים (Jonah 4:8), the witness being את הכיתי אתכם בשדפון ובירקון (Haggai 2:17). Therefore after it: והיו שמיך [your heavens…]; and so in the section אם בחקותי (Leviticus 26)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:12.959866042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}